# Line-ending policy for this repository.
#
# Why this file exists: Git for Windows sets core.autocrlf=true in the system
# gitconfig, so text files were checked out with CRLF on Windows machines.
# gofmt and prettier always emit LF, which made the pre-commit hooks (go-fmt,
# trailing-whitespace, lint-yaml) fail with whole-file CRLF-vs-LF diffs.
# pre-commit's stash/restore cycle made it worse: every restore re-smudged
# working files back to CRLF mid-commit, so even freshly fixed files broke again.
#
# The eol=lf attributes below override core.autocrlf per path: git now writes LF
# on every checkout, stash restore, and branch switch for the file types our
# hooks and formatters rewrite. No local git config changes are needed.
#
# One-time fix for an existing checkout that still has CRLF working files.
# WARNING: discards uncommitted changes — commit or stash everything first:
#   git rm -rfq --cached . && git reset --hard
# (checkout-index/renormalize are not enough: git skips rewriting files whose
# cached stat looks up to date, so the CRLF working copies would survive.)
#
# Deliberately NOT set: a blanket "* text=auto" rule, so that unlisted file
# types keep their current behavior and binary files never depend on git's
# text auto-detection. Add new types to the eol=lf list as needed.

# Go — gofmt emits LF; go-fmt and go-mod-tidy hooks rewrite these
*.go            text eol=lf
go.mod          text eol=lf
go.sum          text eol=lf
*.proto         text eol=lf

# Frontend (Astro + Vue 3 + TypeScript) — prettier emits LF
*.ts            text eol=lf
*.js            text eol=lf
*.mjs           text eol=lf
*.cjs           text eol=lf
*.vue           text eol=lf
*.astro         text eol=lf
*.css           text eol=lf
*.json          text eol=lf
*.arb           text eol=lf

# Config, docs, scripts — trailing-whitespace and lint-yaml (prettier) hooks
*.yml           text eol=lf
*.yaml          text eol=lf
*.yaml.tpl      text eol=lf
*.md            text eol=lf
*.sql           text eol=lf
*.sh            text eol=lf
Makefile        text eol=lf
Dockerfile*     text eol=lf
.gitattributes  text eol=lf
.gitignore      text eol=lf

# Text assets and data files. A handful of these had CRLF committed
# historically (icons under services/kaldheimorg, Turnus CSVs under
# services/pappaperm); they were renormalized to LF when this file landed.
*.svg           text eol=lf
*.csv           text eol=lf
*.html          text eol=lf
*.txt           text eol=lf

# Binary formats git's text auto-detection must never touch. A mostly-ASCII
# PDF (golden fixtures) would otherwise be CRLF-smudged on checkout, which
# corrupts its xref byte offsets.
*.pdf           binary
